          "@type": "IdentificationSpecification",
          "testName": {
            "en": "Identification"
          },
          "testType": "TestType-Identification",
          "testConditions": {
            "en": "Determine the infrared absorption spectrum of L-Methionine, previously dried, as directed in the potas-sium bromide disk method under Infrared Spectrophotome-try <2.25>, and compare the spectrum with the Reference Spectrum: both spectra exhibit similar intensities of absorp-tion at the same wave numbers. D Optical rotation <2.49> [a]20: ＋21.0 – ＋25.09(after dry-ing, 0.5 g, 6 mol/L hydrochloric acid TS, 25 mL, 100 mm). pH <2.54> Dissolve 0.5 g of L-Methionine in 20 mL of water: the pH of this solution is between 5.2 and 6.2."
          }
