            "en": "(1) To a fragment of Agar add dropwise iodine TS: a dark blue to reddish purple color develops. (2) Dissolve 1 g of Agar in 65 mL of water by boiling for 10 minutes with constant stirring, and add a sufficient amount of hot water to make up the water lost by evapora-tion: the solution is clear. Cool the solution between 309C and 399C: the solution forms a firm, resilient gel, which does not melt below 859C."
          }
        },
