      "molecularWeight": 310.39,
      "definition": {
        "en": "Bifonazole, when dried, contains not less than thin-layer chromatography."
      },
      "appearance": {
        "en": "Bifonazole occurs as a white to pale yellow powder. It is odorless and tasteless. It is freely soluble in dichloromethane, soluble in metha-nol, sparingly soluble in ethanol (95), slightly soluble in diethyl ether, and practically insoluble in water. A solution of Bifonazole in methanol (1 in 100) does not show optical rotation."
