      "appearance": {
        "en": "Bismuth Subnitrate occurs as a white powder. It is practically insoluble in water, in ethanol (95) and in diethyl ether. It readily dissolves in hydrochloric acid and in nitric acid without effervescence. It is slightly hygroscopic, and changes moistened blue litmus paper to red."
