          "testConditions": {
            "en": "(1) Heavy metals <1.07>—Prepare the test solution with 1.0 g of the dry extract (or an amount of the viscous ex-tract, equivalent to 1.0 g of the dried substance) as directed under Extracts (4), and perform the test (not more than 30 ppm). (2) Arsenic <1.11>—Prepare the test solution with 0.67 g of the dry extract (or an amount of the viscous extract, equivalent to 0.67 g of the dried substance) according to Method 3, and perform the test (not more than 3 ppm). Loss on drying <2.41> The dry extract: Not more than 11.0z (1 g, 1059C, 5 hours). The viscous extract: Not more than 66.7z (1 g, 1059C, 5 hours). Total ash <5.01> Not less than 8.0z, calculated on the dried basis. However, for the dry extract prepared by adding Light Anhydrous Silicic Acid, between 9.0z and 18.0z."
