as long as the retention time of ciclosporin, beginning after the solvent peak. System suitability— C62H N11O 12: 1202.61 System performance: Proceed as directed in the system suitability in the Assay. cyclo{-[(2S,3R,4R,6E )-3-Hydroxy-4-methyl-2- methylaminooct-6-enoyl]-L-2-aminobutanoyl- N-methylglycyl-N-methyl-L-leucyl-L-valyl-N-methyl- L-leucyl-L-alanyl-D-alanyl-N-methyl-L-leucyl-N-methyl-L-leucyl-N-methyl-L-valyl-} [59865-13-3] Ciclosporin contains not less than 98.5z and not Test for required detectability: To exactly 2 mL of the standard solution add a mixture of water and acetonitrile (1:1) to make exactly 20 mL. Confirm that the peak area of ciclosporin obtained from 20 mL of this solution is equiva-lent to 7 to 13z of that of ciclosporin obtained from 20 mL of the standard solution. System repeatability: When the test is repeated 6 times more than 101.5z of ciclosporin (C 62H111 N11 O12 ), cal- with 20 mL of the standard solution under the above operat- ing conditions, the relative standard deviation of the peak ‌JP XVIII Official Monographs / Cilastatin Sodium 753 area of ciclosporin is not more than 3.0z. Loss on drying <2.41> Not more than 2.0z (1 g, in vacuum at a pressure not exceeding 0.67 kPa, 609C, 3 hours). Residue on ignition <2.44> Not more than 0.1z (0.5 g)."
