        "en": "Clonazepam occurs as white to light yellow, crystals or crystalline powder. It is sparingly soluble in acetic anhydride and in acetone, slightly soluble in methanol and in ethanol (95), very slightly soluble in diethyl ether, and practically insoluble in water. It is gradually colored by light. Melting point: about 2409C (with decomposition)."
