            "en": "Dissolve 0.1 g of d-Camphor in 2 mL of methanol, add 1 mL of 2,4-dinitrophenylhydradine TS, and heat for 5 minutes on a water bath: an orange-red precipitate is formed. D Optical rotation <2.49> [a]20: ＋41.0 – ＋43.09(5 g, ethanol System repeatability: When the test is repeated 6 times with 2 mL of the standard solution under the above operating conditions, the relative standard deviation of the ratios of the peak area of d-camphor to that of the internal standard is not more than 1.0z."
