          "testType": "TestType-Identification",
          "testConditions": {
            "en": "(1) Determine the 1H spectrum of a solu-tion of Eribulin Mesilate in deuterated methanol for nuclear magnetic resonance spectroscopy (1 in 200), as directed under Nuclear Magnetic Resonance Spectroscopy <2.21>, using light hydrogen contaminated in deuterated methanol for nuclear magnetic resonance spectroscopy as an internal reference compound and the chemical shift of methyl group of deuterated methanol as d 3.3 ppm: it exhibits a doublet signal A at around d 1.1 ppm, a multiplet signal B at around d 2.7 ppm and a singlet signal C at around d 2.7 ppm, a singlet signal D at around d 3.4 ppm, a doublet signal E at around d 3.7 ppm, a doublet signal F at around d 4.5 ppm, a triplet signal G at around d 4.6 ppm, and a triplet signal H at around d 4.7 ppm. The ratio of integrated intensity of these signals, A:B ＋ C:D:E:F:G:H, is about 3:5:3:1:1:1:1. (When measured with a nuclear magnetic resonance spectrometer having 1H resonance frequency of not less than or equal to 400 MHz.) (2) Perform the test with 15 mL each of the sample solu-tion and standard solution obtained in the Assay (2) as di-rected under Liquid Chromatography <2.01> according to the following conditions: the retention times of the peaks of methanesulfonic acid in the chromatograms obtained from the sample solution and standard solution are the same. Operating conditions— Proceed as directed in the operating conditions in the Assay (2). System suitability— Proceed as directed in the system suitability in the Assay (2). Optical rotation <2.49> [a]20 : －160 – －2109(50 mg calcu-lated on the anhydrous and solvent-free basis, dimethylsul-foxide, 10 mL, 100 mm)."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "PuritySpecification",
          "testName": {
            "en": "Purity"
          },
          "testType": "TestType-Purity",
          "testConditions": {
            "en": "(1) Heavy metals—Being specified separately when the drug is granted approval based on the Law. Related substances—Weigh accurately about 20 mg of Eribulin Mesilate, dissolve in the dissolving solution to make exactly 5 mL, and use this solution as the sample solu-tion. Separately, weigh accurately about 20 mg of Eribulin Mesilate RS (separately determine the water <2.48> in the same manner as Eribulin Mesilate), dissolve in the dissolving solution to make exactly 5 mL. Pipet 1 mL of this solution, add the dissolving solution to make exactly 100 mL, and use this solution as the standard solution. Perform the test with exactly 5 mL each of the sample solution and standard solu-tion as directed under Liquid Chromatography <2.01> ac-cording to the following conditions. Determine each peak area, AT, of the related substances in the sample solution and the peak area, AS, of eribulin in the standard solution by the automatic integration method, and calculate the amounts of the related substances by the following formula: the amounts of related substance A having the relative reten-tion time of about 0.29 to eribulin, related substance B hav-ing the relative retention time of about 0.87, related sub-stance C having the relative retention time of about 1.07, related substance D having the relative retention time of about 1.29, related substance E having the relative retention time of about 1.37, and related substance F having the rela-tive retention time of about 1.67, are not more than 0.15z, 0.22z, 0.68z, 0.50z, 0.15z, and 0.19z, respectively, and other related substances are not more than 0.10z. Further-more, the total amount of these related substances is not more than 3.0z. Amount (z) of related substance ＝ MS/MT × AT/AS MS: Amount (mg) of Eribulin Mesilate RS taken, calcu- lated on the anhydrous basis MT: Amount (mg) of Eribulin Mesilate taken, calculated on the anhydrous basis Dissolving solution—A mixture of water, acetonitrile for liq-uid chromatography and phosphoric acid (6500:3500:7) adjusted to pH 6.9 – 7.1 with diluted ammonium water (28) (1 in 5) or 1 mol/L hydrochloric acid TS. Operating conditions— Detector, column, column temperature, mobile phase, and flow rate: Proceed as directed in the operating conditions in the Assay (1). Time span of measurement: For 85 minutes after injec-tion, beginning after the solvent peak. System suitability— System performance: Proceed as directed in the system suitability in the Assay (1). Test for required detectability: Pipet 1 mL of the standard solution, and add the dissolving solution to make exactly 20 mL. Confirm that the peak area of eribulin obtained with 5 mL of this solution is equivalent to 3.5 to 6.5z of that with 5 mL of the standard solution. System repeatability: When the test is repeated 5 times with 5 mL of the solution for system suitability test obtained in the Assay (1) under the above operating conditions, the relative standard deviation of the peak area of eribulin is not more than 1.0z. Residual solvent—Being specified separately when the drug is granted approval based on the Law. Water <2.48> Not more than 3.0z (Weigh accurately 15-25 mg of Eribulin Mesilate, dissolve in 2.5 mL of methanol for water determination, and perform the test with exactly 1 mL of this solution; coulometric titration)."
          }
        },
