            "en": "(1) Heavy metals <1.07>—Proceed with 1.0 g of Josamycin Propionate according to Method 2, and perform the test. Prepare the control solution with 3.0 mL of Stand-ard Lead Solution (not more than 30 ppm). Related substances—Dissolve 50 mg of Josamycin Propionate in the mobile phase to make 50 mL, and use this System performance: Dissolve 5 mg of Josamycin Pro-pionate and 2 mg of josamycin in 50 mL of the mobile phase. When the procedure is run with 10 mL of this solution under the above operating conditions, josamycin and josamycin propionate are eluted in this order with the resolu-tion between these peaks being not less than 25. System repeatability: When the test is repeated 6 times with 10 mL of the solution for system suitability test under the above operating conditions, the relative standard devia-tion of the peak area of josamycin propionate is not more than 1.5z. Loss on drying <2.41> Not more than 1.0z (1 g, in vacu-um, phosphorus (V) oxide, 609C, 3 hours). Residue on ignition <2.44> Not more than 0.1z (1 g)."
