      "version": "18",
      "definition": {
        "en": "Povidone-Iodine is a complex of iodine with 1-vinyl- K ＝ ＋ 0.15 ＋ 0.003 c 0.15 c ＋ 0.003 c2 pyrrolidone polymer. c: Mass (g) of Povidone in 100 mL of the solution, calcu-lated on the anhydrous basis It contains not less than 9."
      },
      "appearance": {
        "en": "Povidone-Iodine occurs as a dark red-brown powder. It has a faint, characteristic odor. Nominal K-value calculated on anhydrous basis It is freely soluble in water and in ethanol (99.5). The pH of a solution obtained by dissolving 1.0 g of Povidone-Iodine in 100 mL of water is between 1.5 and 3.5. Not more than 18 5.00 More than 18 and not more than 95 1.00 More than 95 0.10 The K-value is not less than 85z and not more than 115.0z of the nominal K-value when the nominal K-value is not more than 15, and the K-value is not less than 90.0z and not more than 108.0z of the nominal K-value when the nominal K-value is more than 15."
