 0.40 mL of 0.005 mol/L sulfuric acid VS (not more than 0.048z). Heavy metals <1.07>—Proceed with 2.0 g of Praze- pam according to Method 2, and perform the test. Prepare the control solution with 2.0 mL of Standard Lead Solution (not more than 10 ppm). Arsenic <1.11>—Prepare the test solution with 1.0 g of Prazepam according to Method 3, and perform the test (not more than 2 ppm). Related substances—Dissolve 0.40 g of Prazepam in 10 mL of acetone, and use this solution as the sample solu- ometric titration). Perform a blank determination in the same manner, and make any necessary correction. Each mL of 0.1 mol/L perchloric acid VS ＝ 32.48 mg of C19H17ClN2O"
