            "en": "(1) Determine the absorption spectrum of a solution of Ritodrine Hydrochloride in 0.01 mol/L hydro-chloric acid TS (1 in 20,000) as directed under Ultraviolet- Amount (mg) of risperidone (C ＝ MS × AT/AS × 1/25 23H27FN4O2) visible Spectrophotometry <2.24>, and compare the spectrum with the Reference Spectrum or the spectrum of a solution of Ritodrine Hydrochloride RS prepared in the same manner as MS: Amount (mg) of risperidone for assay taken, calcu-lated on the dried basis Operating conditions— Detector: An ultraviolet absorption photometer (wave-length: 275 nm). Column: A stainless steel column 3.0 mm in inside diame-ter and 15 cm in length, packed with octadecylsilanized silica gel for liquid chromatography (3.5 mm in particle diameter). Column temperature: A constant temperature of about 259C. Mobile phase: To 1000 mL of a mixture of water and acetonitrile (4:1) add 1.5 mL of trifluoroacetic acid, and adjust to pH 3.0 with ammonia solution (28). Flow rate: Adjust so that the retention time of risperidone is about 13 minutes. System suitability— System performance: When the procedure is run with 10 mL of the standard solution under the above operating con-ditions, the number of theoretical plates and the symmetry factor of the peak of risperidone are not less than 4000 and not more than 2.5, respectively. System repeatability: When the test is repeated 6 times with 10 mL of the standard solution under the above operat-ing conditions, the relative standard deviation of the peak area of risperidone is not more than 1.0z."
          }
        },
        {
