            "en": "Weigh accurately about 0.2 g of Tizanidine Hydro-chloride, previously dried, dissolve in 60 mL of a mixture of acetic anhydride and acetic acid (100) (7:3) with the aid of warming. After cooling, titrate <2.50> with 0.1 mol/L per-chloric acid VS (potentiometric titration). Perform a blank determination in the same manner, and make any necessary correction. Each mL of 0.1 mol/L perchloric acid VS ＝ 29.02 mg of C9H8ClN5S.HCl"
