      "prefLabel": {
        "en": "Gentianae Radix",
        "ja": "ゲンチアナ"
      },
      "monographId": "JP18-gentianae-radix",
      "publisher": "JP",
      "status": "Official",
      "version": "18",
      "appearance": {
        "en": "Nearly cylindrical pieces, 10 – 50 cm in length, 2 – 4 cm in diameter; externally dark brown; the rhizome short, with fine, transverse wrinkles, and sometimes with ‌2008‌ Powdered Gentian / Crude Drugs and Related Drugs buds and remains of leaves at the upper edge. The root lon-gitudinally and deeply wrinkled, and more or less twisted; fractured surface yellow-brown and not fibrous, and a cam-bium and its neighborhood tinged dark brown. Odor, characteristic; taste, sweet at first, later persistently bitter. Under a microscope <5.01>, a transverse section of the root reveals several cellular layers of collenchyma adjoined internally to 4 to 6 cellular layers of thin-walled cork; secondary cortex with irregularly distributed phloem; xylem consisting chiefly of parenchyma, with individual or clustered vessels and tracheids, and exhibiting some sieve tubes of xylem; parenchyma of the xylem and the cortex con-taining oil droplets, minute needle crystals of calcium oxa-late and very rarely starch grains 10 – 20 mm in diameter."
      },
