loric acid TS to make exactly 100 mL, and use this solution as the standard solution. De- ＝ MS × QT/QS 8 11 5 3 termine the absorbances, AT and AS, at 255 nm of the sam-ple solution and standard solution as directed under Ultravi-olet-visible Spectrophotometry <2.24>, using 0.1 mol/L hy-drochloric acid TS as the blank. Amount (mg) of acyclovir (C8H11N5O3) ＝ MS × AT/AS × 4 MS: Amount (mg) of Aciclovir RS taken, calculated on the anhydrous basis"
