      "publisher": "JP",
      "status": "Official",
      "version": "18",
      "definition": {
        "en": "Azathioprine Tablets contain not less than 95.0z and not more than 105.0z of the labeled amount of azathioprine (C9H7N7O2S: 277.26). Method of preparation Prepare as directed under Tablets, with Azathioprine. Identification (1) Weigh a quantity of powdered Azathioprine Tablets, equivalent to 0.01 g of Azathioprine. Add 50 mL of water, shake well while warming, and filter. Proceed with 5 mL of the filtrate as directed in the Identifi-cation (1) under Azathioprine. Proceed with 1 mL of the filtrate obtained in (1) as directed in the Identification (2) under Azathioprine. Determine the absorption spectrum of the sample so-lution in the Assay as directed under Ultraviolet-visible Spec-trophotometry <2.24>: it exhibits a maximum between 278 nm and 282 nm. Weigh a quantity of powdered Azathioprine Tablets, equivalent to 0.1 g of Azathioprine to the labeled amount. Add 10 mL of a solution of ammonia solution (28) in ethanol (95) (1 in 10), shake well, filter, and use the filtrate MS: Amount (mg) of Azathioprine RS taken Dissolution <6.10> When the test is performed at 50 revolu-tions per minute according to the Paddle method, using 900 mL of water as the dissolution medium, the dissolution rate in 45 minutes of Azathioprine Tablets is not less than 80z. Start the test with 1 tablet of Azathioprine Tablets, with-draw not less than 20 mL of the medium at the specified minute after starting the test, and filter through a membrane filter with a pore size not exceeding 0.8 mm. Discard not less than 10 mL of the first filtrate, pipet V mL of the subsequent filtrate, add water to make exactly V? mL so that each mL contains about 11 mg of azathioprine (C9H7N7O2S), and use this solution as the sample solution."
      },
      "testSpecification": [
