        "en": "Gati‰oxacin Ophthalmic Solution is a clear, pale yellow liquid. Identiˆcation To a volume of Gati‰oxacin Ophthalmic So-lution, equivalent to 6 mg of gati‰oxacin (C19H22FN3O4), add diluted sodium hydroxide TS (1 in 10) to make 30 mL. To 1 mL of this solution add diluted sodium hydroxide TS (1 in 10) to make 20 mL, and determine the absorption spec-trum of this solution as directed under Ultraviolet-visible Spectrophotometry <2.24>: it exhibits maxima between 238 nm and 242 nm, between 287 nm and 291 nm, and between 336 nm and 340 nm. Osmotic pressure ratio Being speciˆed separately when the drug is granted approval based on the Law. pH Being speciˆed separately when the drug is granted approval based on the Law."
