ed at 1059C for 2 hours, dissolve in water to make exactly 100 mL, then pipet 5 mL of this solution, add water to make exactly 50 mL, and then pipet 5 mL of this solution, add water to make exactly 50 mL, and use this solution as the standard solution. Determine the absorbances, AT and AS, of the sample solu-tion and standard solution at 267 nm as directed under Ultraviolet-visible Spectrophotometry <2.24>. Dissolution rate (z) with respect to the labeled amount of isoniazid (C6H7N3O) ＝ MS × AT/AS × 1/C × 90 MS: Amount (mg) of isoniazid for assay taken C: Labeled amount (mg) of isoniazid (C6H7N3O) in 1 tablet"
