est with 1 tablet of Pentobarbital Calcium Tablets, withdraw not less than 20 mL of the medium at the specified minute after starting the test, and filter through a membrane filter with a pore size not exceeding 0.45 mm. Dis-card not less than 10 mL of the first filtrate, pipet V mL of the subsequent filtrate, add the dissolution medium to make exactly V? mL so that each mL contains about 56 mg of pen-tobarbital calcium (C22H34CaN4O6). Pipet 3 mL of this solu-tion, add dilute sodium hydroxide TS to make exactly 10 mL, and use this solution as the sample solution. Separately, weigh accurately about 26 mg of Pentobarbital RS, previ-ously dried at 1059C for 2 hours, dissolve in 2 mL of ethanol (99.5), and add water to make exactly 100 mL. Pipet 4 mL of this solution, and add the dissolution medium to make ex-actly 20 mL. Pipet 3 mL of this solution, add dilute sodium hydroxide TS to make exactly 10 mL, and use this solution as the standard solution. Determine the absorbances, AT and AS, of the sample solution and standard solution at 241 nm as directed under Ultraviolet-visible Spectrophotometry <2.24>, using a solution, prepared by adding dilute sodium hydroxide TS to 3 mL of the dissolution medium to make 10 mL, as the blank. Dissolution rate (z) with respect to the labeled amount of pentobarbital calcium (C22H34CaN4O6) ＝ MS × AT/AS × V?/V × 1/C × 180 × 1.084 MS: Amount (mg) of Pentobarbital RS taken C: Labeled amount (mg) of pentobarbital calcium (C22H34CaN4O6) in 1 tablet"
