e method, using 900 mL of 2nd fluid for dissolution test as the dissolution medium, the dissolution rate in 90 minutes of Perphenazine Tablets is not less than 70z. Start the test with 1 tablet of Perphenazine Tablets, withdraw not less than 20 mL of the medium at the specified minute after starting the test, and filter through a membrane filter with a pore size not exceeding 0.8 mm. Discard not less than 10 mL of the first filtrate, and use the subsequent fil-trate as the sample solution. Separately, weigh accurately about 10 mg of Perphenazine RS, previously dried in vacu-um with phosphorus (V) oxide at 659C for 4 hours, dissolve in 5 mL of 0.1 mol/L hydrochloric acid TS, and add the dis-solution medium to make exactly 250 mL. Pipet 5 mL of this solution, add the dissolution medium to make exactly 100 mL, and use this solution as the standard solution. Deter-mine the absorbances, AT and AS, of the sample solution and standard solution at 255 nm as directed under Ultravio-let-visible Spectrophotometry <2.24>. Dissolution rate (z) with respect to the labeled amount of perphenazine (C21H26ClN3OS) ＝ MS × AT/AS × 1/C × 18 MS: Amount (mg) of Perphenazine RS taken C: Labeled amount (mg) of perphenazine (C21H26ClN3OS) in 1 tablet"
