            "en": "Weigh accurately and powder not less than 20 Propiverine Hydrochloride Tablets. Weigh accurately a por-tion of the powder, equivalent to about 50 mg of propiverine hydrochloride (C23H29NO3.HCl), add the mobile phase, shake vigorously, and add the mobile phase to make exactly 100 mL. Centrifuge this solution, pipet 10 mL of the super-natant liquid, add the mobile phase to make exactly 50 mL, and use this solution as the sample solution. Separately, weigh accurately about 50 mg of Propiverine Hydrochloride RS, previously dried at 1059C for 1 hour, and dissolve in the mobile phase to make exactly 100 mL. Pipet 10 mL of this solution, add the mobile phase to make exactly 50 mL, and use this solution as the standard solution. Then, proceed as directed in the Assay under Propiverine Hydrochloride. Amount (mg) of propiverine hydrochloride (C23H29NO3.HCl) ＝ MS × AT/AS MS: Amount (mg) of Propiverine Hydrochloride RS taken"
