        "en": "Purified Sodium Hyaluronate Injection",
        "ja": "精製ヒアルロン酸ナトリウム注射液"
      },
      "monographId": "JP18-purified-sodium-hyaluronate-injection",
      "publisher": "JP",
      "status": "Official",
      "version": "18",
      "definition": {
        "en": "Purified Sodium Hyaluronate Injection is an aque-ous injection. It contains not less than 90."
      },
      "appearance": {
        "en": "Purified Sodium Hyaluronate Injection occurs as a clear, colorless, and viscous liquid."
      },
      "testSpecification": [
        {
          "@type": "IdentificationSpecification",
          "testName": {
            "en": "Identification"
          },
          "testType": "TestType-Identification",
          "testConditions": {
            "en": "(1) To 1 mL of a solution of Purified So-dium Hyaluronate Injection (1 in 10) add 6 mL of sulfuric acid, and heat in a water bath for 10 minutes. After cooling, add 0.2 mL of carbazole TS, and allow to stand at room temperature: a red to red-purple color develops. To 1 mL of a solution of Purified Sodium Hyaluronate Injection (1 in 10) add 0.2 mL of 1 mol/L acetic acid-sodium acetate buffer solution (pH 6.0) and 5 units of hyaluronidase, and allow to stand at 509C for 1 hour. To this solution add 1 mL of a solution of dipotassium tetraborate tetrahydrate (1 in 20), heat in a water bath for Average molecular mass ＝ 0.78 7 minutes. After cooling, add 6 mL of acetic acid (100) and In the case of the labeled average molecular mass of between 1,500,000 and 3,900,000. Calculate the average molecular mass of Purified Sodium Hyaluronate according to the following equation: it is be-tween 1,500,000 and 3,900,000. For [h], use the maximum viscosity under Viscosity. Ø[h] × 105 »   1    2.4 mL of 4-dimethylaminobenzaldehyde-hydrochloric acid-acetic acid TS, and allow to stand at room temperature: a yellowish red to red color develops. To 1 mL of a solution of Purified Sodium Hyaluronate Injection (1 in 10) add 2 to 3 drops of a solution of cetylpyridinium chloride monohydrate (1 in 20): a white precipitate is formed. Average molecular mass ＝ 22.8 0.816 Viscosity <2.53> Apply to the preparation which labeled average mo- ‌lecular mass of sodium hyaluronate is 600,000 to 1,200,000. Weigh accurately an amount of Purified Sodium Hyaluronate Injection, equivalent to about 10 mg of Puri-fied Sodium Hyaluronate, add 0.2 mol/L sodium chloride TS to make exactly 20 mL, and use this solution as the sam-ple solution. Perform the test with the sample solution at 30 ± 0.19C according to Method 1, using an Ubbelohde-type"
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "AssaySpecification",
          "testName": {
            "en": "Assay"
          },
          "testType": "TestType-Assay",
          "testConditions": {
            "en": "Weigh accurately an amount of Purified Sodium Hyaluronate Injection, equivalent to about 10 mg of Puri-fied Sodium Hyaluronate, and add 0.2 mol/L sodium chlo-ride TS to make exactly 20 mL. Pipet 1 mL of this solution, add water to make exactly 10 mL, and use this solution as the sample solution. Then, proceed as directed in the Assay under Purified Sodium Hyaluronate. viscometer showing the downflowing time of 0.2 mol/L so- dium chloride TS is between 200 and 300 seconds. Calculate Content (mg) of sodium hyaluronate [(C14H20 NNaO11)n] the intrinsic viscosity [h] according to the following equa-tion, where c is the content obtained in the Assay expressed as the concentration (g/dL): 11.8 – 19.5 dL/g. per mL of Purified Sodium Hyaluronate Injection ＝ MS/MT × AT/AS × 1/5 × r × 2.279 MS: Amount (mg) of D-Glucuronolactone RS taken [h] ＝ 2(hsp － ln h rel)/c × 0.87 ＋ 1.33 MT: Amount (g) of Purified Sodium Hyaluronate Injec-tion taken hsp (specific viscosity) ＝ hrel － 1 hrel (relative viscosity) ＝ t/t0 Apply to the preparation which labeled average molecular mass of sodium hyaluronate is 1,500,000 to 2,000,000. Weigh accurately an amount of Purified Sodium Hyaluronate Injection, equivalent to about 4 mg of Purified Sodium Hyaluronate, add 0.2 mol/L sodium chloride TS to make exactly 20 mL, and use this solution as the sample solution. Perform the test with the sample solution at 30 ± 0.19C according to Method 1, using an Ubbelohde-type vis-cometer showing the downflowing time of 0.2 mol/L sodium chloride TS is between 200 and 300 seconds. Calculate the intrinsic viscosity [h] according to the following equation: 24.5 – 31.5 dL/g. r: Density (g/mL) of Purified Sodium Hyaluronate Injec-tion measured as directed under Determination of Specific Gravity and Density <2.56>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "storageConditions": {
        "en": "Containers—Hermetic containers. Plastic containers for aqueous injections may be used."
      },
      "dosageForm": "Injection"
    },
    {
      "@context": "https://www.openphar.org/ontology/context/pharmacopoeia.jsonld",
      "@id": "https://www.openphar.org/data/jp/formulations/purified-sodium-hyaluronate-ophthalmic-solution",
      "@type": "FormulationMonograph",
      "prefLabel": {
        "en": "Purified Sodium Hyaluronate Ophthalmic Solution",
        "ja": "精製ヒアルロン酸ナトリウム点眼液"
      },
      "monographId": "JP18-purified-sodium-hyaluronate-ophthalmic-solution",
      "publisher": "JP",
      "status": "Official",
      "version": "18",
      "definition": {
        "en": "Purified Sodium Hyaluronate Ophthalmic Solution 1 － 0.432・ln hrel [h] ＝ (1 － hrel (relative viscosity) ＝ t/t0 )/(0.0108 × M ) is an aqueous ophthalmic preparation. It contains not less than 90."
      },
      "appearance": {
        "en": "Purified Sodium Hyaluronate Ophthalmic So-lution occurs as a clear, colorless, and viscous liquid."
      },
      "testSpecification": [
        {
          "@type": "IdentificationSpecification",
          "testName": {
            "en": "Identification"
          },
          "testType": "TestType-Identification",
          "testConditions": {
            "en": "(1) To 1 mL of Purified Sodium Hyaluronate Ophthalmic Solution add 0.2 mL of 1 mol/L acetic acid-sodium acetate buffer solution (pH 6.0) and 5 units of hyaluronidase, and allow to stand at 509C for 1 hour. Add 1 mL of a solution of dipotassium tetraborate tetrahydrate (1 in 20), and heat in a water bath for 7 minutes. After cooling, add 6 mL of acetic acid (100) and 2.4 mL of 4-dimethylaminobenzaldehyde-hydrochloric acid-acetic acid TS, and allow to stand at room temperature: a yellowish red to red color develops. (2) To 1 volume of Purified Sodium Hyaluronate Oph-thalmic Solution, equivalent to 7.5 mg of purified sodium hyaluronate [(C14H20NNaO11)n], add 2 volumes of acetone, shake well, and centrifuge at 3000 rpm for 10 minutes. Re-move the acetone, wash the precipitate with a mixture of ace-tone and water (5:1), dry the precipitate under reduced pres-sure (not exceeding 0.67 kPa) at 609C for 5 hours using phosphorus (V) oxide as a desiccant, and determine the in- Average molecular mass ＝ 0.78 frared absorption spectrum as directed in ATR method Apply to the preparation which labeled average mo-lecular mass of sodium hyaluronate is 1,500,000 to 2,000,000. Calculate the average molecular mass by the following equa-tion, where [h] is the intrinsic viscosity obtained in the Vis-cosity: it is 1,500,000 to 2,000,000. Ø[h] × 105 »   1    under Infrared Spectrophotometry <2.25>: it exhibits absorp-tion at the wave numbers of about 1605 cm－1, 1404 cm－1, 1375 cm－1, 1150 cm－1, 1025 cm－1 and 945 cm－1. Osmotic pressure ratio Being specified separately when the drug is granted approval based on the Law. pH Being specified separately when the drug is granted ap-proval based on the Law. Average molecular mass ＝ 22.8 0.816 ‌Viscosity <2.53> Perform the test according to Method 1 at 30 ± 0.19C: the kinematic viscosity is 3.0 to 4.0 mm2/s or 17 to 30 mm2/s. Foreign insoluble matter <6.11> It meets the requirement. Insoluble particulate matter <6.08> It meets the require-ment. Sterility <4.06> Perform the test according to the Mem-brane filtration method: it meets the requirement. Average molecular mass When determined by the follow-ing method it is between 600,000 and 1,200,000. Determination of viscosity <2.53> Weigh accurately an amount of Purified Sodium Hyaluronate Ophthalmic Solution, equivalent to about 15 mg of purified sodium hyaluronate [(C14H20NNaO11)n], add 0.2 mol/L sodium chloride TS to make exactly 30 mL, and use this solution as the sample solution. Perform the test with the sample solution according to Method 1 at 30 ± 0.19C, using an Ubbelohde-type viscometer with the down-flowing time of 0.2 mol/L sodium chloride TS is between 200 and 300 seconds. Calculate the intrinsic viscosity [h] according to the following equation, where c is the content obtained in the Assay expressed as the concentration (g/dL): 11.8 – 19.5 dL/g. [h] ＝ 2(hsp － ln hrel)/c × 0.87 ＋ 1.33 hsp (specific viscosity) ＝ hrel － 1 hrel (relative e viscosity) ＝ t/t0 Calculation of average molecular mass Calculate by the following equation, using the intrinsic viscosity obtained in (i) for [h]. Ø[h] × 105 »  1    Flow rate: Adjust so that the retention time of hyaluronic acid is about 5 minutes. System suitability— System performance: Dissolve 50 mg of purified sodium hyaluronate in 50 mL of sodium chloride solution (9 in 1000). To 1 mL of this solution and 2 mL of a solution of e-aminocaproic acid (1 in 500) add the mobile phase to make 20 mL, and use this solution as the solution for system suitability test. When the procedure is run with 20 mL of the solution for system suitability test under the above operating conditions, hyaluronic acid and e-aminocaproic acid are eluted in this order with the resolution between these peaks being not less than 5. System repeatability: When the test is repeated 6 times with 20 mL of the standard solution under the above operat-ing conditions, the relative standard deviation of the peak area of hyaluronic acid is not more than 2.0z."
          }
        }
      ],
      "storageConditions": {
        "en": "Containers—Tight containers."
      },
      "dosageForm": "Solution"
    },
    {
      "@context": "https://www.openphar.org/ontology/context/pharmacopoeia.jsonld",
      "@id": "https://www.openphar.org/data/jp/formulations/quetiapine-fumarate-fine-granules",
      "@type": "FormulationMonograph",
      "prefLabel": {
        "en": "Quetiapine Fumarate Fine Granules",
        "ja": "クエチアピンフマル酸塩細粒"
