        "en": "Sodium Valproate Extended-release Tablets B con- ＝ MS × A ＋ ∑ i＝1 ×  AS 45 × × × 360 V C tain not less than 95.0z and not more than 105.0z of the labeled amount of sodium valproate (C8H15NaO2: 166.19). Method of preparation Prepare as directed under Tablets, with Sodium Valproate. Identiˆcation To a quantity of the powdered Sodium Val-proate Extended-release Tablets B, equivalent to 1.0 g of So-dium Valproate, add 10 mL of water, heat on a water bath for 30 minutes, and ˆlter. To 2.5 mL of the ˆltrate add 2.5 mL of water and 1 mL of a solution of cobalt (II) nitrate hexahydrate (1 in 20), and heat on a water bath: a purple precipitate is formed. Uniformity of dosage units <6.02> Perform the Mass varia-tion test, or the Content uniformity test according to the fol-lowing method: it meets the requirement. To 1 tablet of Sodium Valproate Extended-release Tablets B add 150 mL of the mobile phase, allow to stand for not less than 16 hours, shake until the ˆlm is disintegrated, and add the mobile phase to make exactly 200 mL. Pipet V mL of this solution, and add the mobile phase to make exactly V? mL so that each mL contains about 1 mg of sodium val-proate (C8H15NaO2)."
