ed on the Law. gel for liquid chromatography (5 mm in particle diameter). Column temperature: A constant temperature of about 509C. Mobile phase: A mixture of water, 2-propanol for liquid chromatography and tetrahydrofuran for liquid chromatog-raphy (5:2:2). Flow rate: Adjust so that the retention time of tacrolimus is about 10 minutes. ‌System suitability— System performance: When the procedure is run with 10 mL of the standard solution under the above operating con-ditions, tacrolimus and the internal standard are eluted in this order with the resolution between these peaks being not less than 6, and the number of theoretical plates and the symmetry factor of the peak of tacrolimus are not less than 3000 and not more than 1.5, respectively. System repeatability: When the test is repeated 5 times with 10 mL of the standard solution under the above operat-ing conditions, the relative standard deviation of the ratio of the peak area of tacrolimus to that of the internal standard is not more than 1.0z."
